admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":113,"created_at":"2026-10-25T05:45:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T16:20:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-12T16:20:49Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## What and why\n\nRoute builder and moderator authority through the session frames. Today the install and revoke frames do not carry a builder or moderator actor. Phase 12 (PR #801, F12.3) added the `BUILDER`/`MODERATOR` scope bits, `invite --role builder|moderator`, and the journal-only audit entries `BuilderInstalled` and `Revoked { by }`. But every caller passes `by: None`, so in practice a builder cannot install and a moderator cannot revoke over the wire, and the audit entries never appear. PR #801 lists \"F12.3 install/revoke frame wiring\" as remaining, and no issue tracks it.\n\n## Source\n\n- [Phase 14 plan](https://github.com/developing-today/code/blob/main/.opencode/plans/phase-14-close-out.md): F14.6 (PR #834)\n- [Phase 12 plan](https://github.com/developing-today/code/blob/main/.opencode/plans/phase-12-platform-flexibility.md): F12.3\n- PR #801 body, \"Remaining Phase 12\": \"F12.3 install/revoke frame wiring\"\n- Epic #534, D1-021\n\n## Current status\n\n**Partial.** `pkgs/id/src/world/handle.rs:489` (`revoke` → `revoke_by(participant_id, None)`) and `:648` (`install_program` → `install_program_by(..., None, ...)`) are the only callers of the `_by` variants outside tests. `world/actor.rs:1192-1195` journals `BuilderInstalled` only when an actor is passed. The session code in `world_session/` never passes one.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The install-module frame accepts a participant holding `BUILDER` and passes the actor to `install_program_by`\n- [ ] The revoke frame accepts a participant holding `MODERATOR` and passes the actor to `revoke_by`\n- [ ] Over a real session (not the handle API), a builder installs, a moderator revokes, and a plain guest is refused for both with the documented F11.13 code\n- [ ] Each use is journaled with its actor (`BuilderInstalled`, `Revoked { by }`)\n- [ ] Builder still receives no network, file, or process authority (test)\n\n## Size\n\nM\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- #227: F11.12 journal format version (Phase 14 F14.1). `BuilderInstalled` is a new entry type, and it must be covered by the version contract before it is produced in practice.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://